From 2db8c33f30f7332c94012ec03fe9b0b7ec62680f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AmirSalahY <hello@noury.ch>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 16:40:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/34] fix(frecency): match path suggestions against their own
 history
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Folder and file suggestions reach the ranker as "src/" — the trailing separator
is stripped later, by adjustPathSuggestions — while history records what was
typed, "cd src". The keys therefore never matched, so usage ranking was dead for
every path suggestion regardless of sortMethod. Reported as "cd" listing
directories alphabetically despite `cd nrp` being the most recent command.

Keys are now normalised on both sides, so "cd src/" and "cd src" are one entry.

Also stops the suite writing to the developer's own ~/.inshellisense. Frecency
writes are fire-and-forget, so the previous save-and-restore lost the race — an
append could land after the restore, leaving real history polluted or, if a run
was interrupted, gone. constants.ts now honours ISTERM_RESOURCES_DIR and the
tests point it at a scratch directory.
